    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35931" root="قعث" body-key="q">
    
      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اقعث فِى مَالِهِ</span></b>  <i>He acted extravagantly in
respect of his property.</i> (ISk, S, O, K. *) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اقعث لَهُ العَطِيَّةَ</span> <i>He made the gift to him
large;</i> (S, O, K, TA;) and so ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِقْتَعَثَهَا</span></b> , and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اقعثهُ</span>
[i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اقعثهُ العَطِيَّةَ</span>]. (TA. See the verse cited
voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُقْعَثٌ</span>; and the remark of As respecting it.)

